  "description": "meme-id: anne frankly i don't care; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a historical photograph of Adolf Hitler with the text 'anne frankly i don't care,' creating a darkly humorous and intentionally provocative statement. The phrase 'anne frankly' is a pun on 'Anne Frank,' referencing her famous diary and the Holocaust, while 'i don't care' implies indifference to the suffering and genocide she documented. This meme is hateful because it trivializes the Holocaust and the victims of Nazi persecution by mocking their pain with a tone of apathy. It directly attacks the historical memory of the Holocaust and the moral gravity of the event, using the image of Hitler to symbolize the perpetrator of mass atrocities. The intent is to shock and provoke, but it does so by minimizing the horror of genocide, which is a form of hate speech targeting victims of the Holocaust and their historical legacy.",
